{ SYNTHETIC FIXTURE — NOT the real Analytica model.
  This is a hand-written .ana that mimics the *structure* of the EVIU
  "when to leave for the airport" plane-catching example so tools/ana_to_wasim.py
  can be exercised end-to-end. The real docs.analytica.com file was not
  reachable from this environment (org egress allowlist). Node values here are
  illustrative, not authoritative. }
Softwareversion 6.4

Model Eviu_plane_catching
Title: When to leave for the airport (EVIU, synthetic)
Author: fixture
Description: Choose a departure time trading off waiting at the gate against the cost of missing the plane.
Nodelocation: 100,100,1
Nodesize: 48,24

Decision Depart_early
Title: Minutes to leave before scheduled flight
Units: minutes
Definition: 90
Nodelocation: 100,60,1

Chance Travel_time
Title: Travel time to airport
Units: minutes
Description: Uncertain door-to-gate travel time.
Definition: Lognormal(60, 1.3)
Nodelocation: 220,60,1
Nodesize: 48,24

Constant Boarding_buffer
Title: Boarding buffer before departure
Units: minutes
Definition: 20
Nodelocation: 100,140,1

Constant Wait_cost
Title: Cost per minute waiting at gate
Units: USD/minute
Definition: 0.5

Constant Miss_penalty
Title: Cost of missing the plane
Units: USD
Definition: 400

Variable Slack
Title: Slack on arrival
Units: minutes
Description: Minutes to spare at the gate; negative means the plane was missed.
Definition: Depart_early - Travel_time - Boarding_buffer
Nodelocation: 340,100,1

Variable Cost
Title: Cost of the trip
Units: USD
Definition: If Slack >= 0 Then Wait_cost * Slack Else Miss_penalty
Nodelocation: 460,100,1

Objective Expected_cost
Title: Expected cost
Units: USD
Definition: Mean(Cost)
Nodelocation: 580,100,1

Variable Sampesize
Title: Sample size
Definition: 5000
